  "correct": 2,
  "explanation": "Stratified random sampling involves dividing the population into meaningful subgroups (strata) and then randomly sampling from within each stratum, ensuring representation across important characteristics like socioeconomic status. Simple random sampling selects directly from the entire population without any stratification. Systematic sampling selects every nth individual from a list, without stratification. Cluster sampling randomly selects entire naturally occurring groups (clusters), not individuals stratified by characteristic. Convenience sampling selects readily available subjects without any randomization or stratification, introducing significant selection bias."
