  "explanation": "WHO defines anemia in pregnancy as hemoglobin concentration below 11 g/dL, reflecting the physiological hemodilution that normally occurs during pregnancy alongside true iron and nutritional demands. 15 g/dL is actually within or above the normal non-pregnant adult female hemoglobin range, well above the anemia threshold. 8 g/dL would actually represent moderate-to-severe anemia, a more severe category, not the general threshold for defining anemia itself. 5 g/dL would represent very severe, life-threatening anemia, far below the diagnostic threshold. 18 g/dL is well above normal, actually more consistent with polycythemia, not remotely close to an anemia cutoff."
