        "exp": "Increased body temperature destroys the heat-sensitive germ cells (spermatogonia) and Sertoli cells lining the seminiferous tubules. However, Leydig cells (located in the interstitium) are heat-resistant and are relatively spared, so testosterone levels often remain normal.",
