        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 32-year-old female presents with sudden visual loss in one eye and unilateral arm weakness, which resolve after a few weeks. A year later, she develops a tremor and urinary incontinence. CSF analysis reveals the presence of oligoclonal bands. The primary pathogenesis of her disease involves the destruction of:",
