        "question": "A 50-year-old male presents with a solitary, sharply demarcated, erythematous, crusting plaque on the skin of his scrotum. Biopsy shows large cells with pale, clear cytoplasm scattered within the epidermis. The cells stain positive for PAS, Keratin, and CEA, but negative for S-100. Diagnosis?",
