        "question": "A 2-year-old child who recently recovered from a mild viral URI suddenly develops a high fever, muffled voice ('hot potato voice'), drooling, and leans forward to breathe. You suspect epiglottitis. Why is it strictly contraindicated to use a tongue depressor to examine his throat?",
