        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 35-year-old male undergoes evaluation for a painless testicular nodule. Biopsy reveals a tumor composed of cells resembling syncytiotrophoblasts and cytotrophoblasts, but remarkably, no chorionic villi are formed. The tumor is heavily hemorrhagic and necrotic. What is the diagnosis?",
