        "question": "A 70-year-old male with BPH undergoes a transurethral resection of the prostate (TURP). The microscopic examination of the removed chips of tissue shows nodular hyperplasia of glands and stroma. The glandular spaces frequently contain inspissated, laminated, eosinophilic proteinaceous material. What are these structures called?",
