        "exp": "Achalasia is characterized by the inability of the lower esophageal sphincter to relax and a loss of esophageal peristalsis. It is caused by the destruction of ganglion cells in the myenteric (Auerbach) plexus. In South America, Chagas disease (Trypanosoma cruzi) is a known secondary cause.",
