        "exp": "Barrett esophagus is intestinal metaplasia of the lower esophagus due to chronic acid reflux (GERD). The normal stratified squamous epithelium transforms into non-ciliated columnar epithelium with mucin-producing goblet cells. It carries a massive risk for esophageal adenocarcinoma.",
