        "exp": "Zollinger-Ellison syndrome is caused by a gastrin-secreting tumor (gastrinoma), usually in the pancreas or duodenum, leading to massive acid hypersecretion and refractory ulcers. It is strongly associated with MEN 1 syndrome (Pituitary, Parathyroid, and Pancreatic tumors).",
