        "exp": "Ulcerative Colitis (UC) classically involves the rectum and extends proximally in a continuous fashion. It is restricted to the mucosa and submucosa. The histological hallmark is the crypt abscess (neutrophils accumulating in the crypts of Lieberkühn). Granulomas, transmural inflammation, and 'cobblestoning' are features of Crohn disease.",
        "book": "Kaplan Medical USMLE Step 1 Pathology",
        "subtopic": "Inflammatory Bowel Disease"
