        "topic": "Gastrointestinal",
        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 30-year-old male with a history of recurrent right lower quadrant pain, diarrhea, and a perianal fistula presents for follow-up. He is diagnosed with Crohn disease. What is the most common extraintestinal manifestation that affects the hepatobiliary system in patients with Inflammatory Bowel Disease (IBD), more specifically Ulcerative Colitis, but can also occur in Crohn's?",
