        "topic": "Gastrointestinal",
        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "An elderly woman presents with severe left lower quadrant pain, fever, and leukocytosis. She has a long-standing history of a low-fiber diet. CT scan reveals inflammation of small, flask-like outpouchings in the sigmoid colon. This condition represents an inflammation of 'false' diverticula. What layers of the bowel wall make up a false diverticulum?",
