        "correct": 1,
        "exp": "Diverticulitis is the inflammation of diverticula (most common in the sigmoid colon). These are 'false' (pulsion) diverticula because only the mucosa and submucosa herniate through areas of weakness in the muscularis propria (where the vasa recta penetrate). A 'true' diverticulum (like Meckel's) contains all three layers.",
        "book": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease",
        "subtopic": "Colonic Diverticulosis"
