        "exp": "Meckel diverticulum is a true diverticulum caused by the failure of the omphalomesenteric (vitelline) duct to obliterate. It classically contains ectopic gastric mucosa (which takes up the Tc-99m on a Meckel scan) that secretes acid, ulcerating adjacent bowel and causing painless bleeding.",
