        "exp": "Pseudomembranous colitis is caused by Clostridioides difficile overgrowth after antibiotic use. C. diff produces Toxin A (watery diarrhea) and Toxin B. Toxin B is a cytotoxin that depolymerizes actin by glucosylating Rho GTPases, causing cytoskeletal disruption and necrosis (forming the pseudomembranes).",
