        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 6-month-old infant is brought to the ER with intermittent, severe, colicky abdominal pain. The mother notes that the baby draws his legs up to his chest and passes stool that looks like 'currant jelly.' Ultrasound shows a 'target sign' in the right upper quadrant. This condition is caused by:",
