        "topic": "Hematology",
        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 70-year-old male is found to have asymptomatic massive lymphocytosis on a routine CBC. Peripheral smear reveals numerous small, mature-appearing lymphocytes and frequent 'smudge cells'. Immunophenotyping shows these B-cells aberrantly express the T-cell marker CD5. Diagnosis?",
