        "exp": "Gastric MALTomas (Mucosa-Associated Lymphoid Tissue lymphomas) arise due to chronic immune stimulation by Helicobacter pylori. Amazingly, early-stage MALTomas can completely regress when the H. pylori infection is eradicated with standard triple therapy (antibiotics + PPI).",
        "book": "Kaplan Medical USMLE Step 1 Pathology",
        "subtopic": "Stomach Pathology"
