        "topic": "Breast Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 35-year-old premenopausal female complains of bilateral, lumpy, 'rope-like' breast tissue that becomes tender right before her period. Biopsy shows cysts, fibrosis, and apocrine metaplasia. What is the risk of this specific set of findings progressing to breast carcinoma?",
