        "difficulty": "Harder",
        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 55-year-old male from China is found to have Hepatocellular Carcinoma (HCC). While Hepatitis B is a major risk factor, he has a history of consuming grain contaminated with Aspergillus flavus. The toxin produced by this mold induces HCC by causing a specific mutation. What is the mutated gene?",
