        "exp": "The splenic flexure (Griffith's point) is a classic 'watershed area' where the territories of the Superior Mesenteric Artery (SMA) and Inferior Mesenteric Artery (IMA) meet. In systemic hypotension or severe atherosclerosis, these distal anastomotic areas are the first to suffer ischemic colitis.",
