        "topic": "Gastrointestinal",
        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 25-year-old male is found to have hundreds of adenomatous polyps in his colon. He also has multiple osteomas in his mandible, epidermoid cysts on his skin, and congenital hypertrophy of the retinal pigment epithelium (CHRPE). This specific variant of FAP is known as:",
