        "exp": "Gardner syndrome is an autosomal dominant variant of Familial Adenomatous Polyposis (FAP). It is characterized by FAP plus extraintestinal manifestations: osteomas (benign bone tumors, often in the jaw), fibromatosis, and skin cysts. Turcot syndrome is FAP + CNS tumors (medulloblastoma).",
        "book": "Kaplan Medical USMLE Step 1 Pathology",
        "subtopic": "Polyposis Syndromes"
