        "topic": "Hepatobiliary Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Harder",
        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 60-year-old patient with severe cirrhosis is brought to the hospital confused, lethargic, and demonstrating asterixis (flapping tremor). This hepatic encephalopathy is due to high serum ammonia crossing the blood-brain barrier. Within the brain, which cells primarily take up this ammonia, and what is the toxic byproduct that causes them to swell?",
