        "topic": "Hepatobiliary Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 22-year-old female presents with jaundice, fatigue, and amenorrhea. She has no history of viral hepatitis or alcohol use. Labs show elevated AST and ALT. Serum protein electrophoresis shows hypergammaglobulinemia. Serology is strongly positive for Anti-Smooth Muscle Antibodies (ASMA). Diagnosis?",
