        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 25-year-old medical student gets routine blood work and is found to have a mild, isolated elevation in conjugated (direct) bilirubin. He is completely asymptomatic. A liver biopsy is performed for some reason, and the liver is grossly pitch-black in color. What is the diagnosis?",
