        "topic": "Gastrointestinal",
        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "An 80-year-old nursing home resident presents with massive abdominal distension and obstipation (inability to pass stool or gas). Abdominal X-ray shows a massively dilated loop of large bowel forming a 'coffee bean' sign arising from the left lower quadrant. Diagnosis?",
