        "exp": "Pyloric stenosis presents at 2-6 weeks of life with non-bilious projectile vomiting. Because the infant is vomiting massive amounts of gastric acid (HCl), they develop a hypochloremic metabolic alkalosis. The kidneys attempt to save protons (H+) by excreting potassium, leading to concurrent hypokalemia.",
