        "question": "A 40-year-old female undergoes a routine abdominal ultrasound which incidentally reveals a 3 cm mass in the liver. A contrast CT scan shows a well-circumscribed, spongy, blood-filled mass with peripheral-to-central enhancement. Why is an image-guided biopsy of this lesion strictly CONTRAINDICATED?",
