        "question": "A 2-week-old infant presents with worsening jaundice, dark urine, and pale (acholic) stools. Labs show a massive elevation of direct (conjugated) bilirubin. Ultrasound shows an absent or incredibly small gallbladder. If surgical intervention (Kasai procedure) is not performed, this infant will rapidly develop cirrhosis. Diagnosis?",
