        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 70-year-old critically ill patient recovering from massive trauma and sepsis in the ICU suddenly develops fever, severe right upper quadrant pain, and an elevated WBC count. Ultrasound shows a thickened gallbladder wall and pericholecystic fluid, but NO gallstones are present. What is the pathogenesis of this condition?",
