        "exp": "Acalculous cholecystitis (inflammation of the gallbladder without stones) occurs in critically ill, traumatized, or severely burned patients. It is caused by gallbladder ischemia (from hypotension/shock) combined with biliary stasis (since the patient is not eating enterally, CCK is not released to empty the gallbladder).",
        "book": "Robbins & Cotran Pathologic Basis of Disease",
        "subtopic": "Gallbladder Pathology"
