        "exp": "Spontaneous Bacterial Peritonitis (SBP) is an infection of ascitic fluid without an obvious intra-abdominal source (like a perforated bowel). It is diagnosed when the absolute neutrophil count (ANC) in the fluid is > 250 cells/mm3. Gram-negative enteric bacteria, particularly E. coli and Klebsiella, are the most common pathogens.",
