        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 19-year-old female is brought to the ER after intentionally ingesting a massive dose of an over-the-counter pain reliever. She develops severe acute liver failure. Liver biopsy would show centrilobular necrosis. The toxicity is caused by the depletion of which intracellular antioxidant, allowing the toxic metabolite NAPQI to destroy hepatocytes?",
