        "question": "A 22-year-old medical student develops mild jaundice the week before his final board exams. He feels completely fine otherwise. Labs show a mild, isolated elevation in unconjugated bilirubin. Liver enzymes are completely normal. The jaundice resolves after the exams are over. What is the diagnosis?",
