        "question": "A 65-year-old female with a long history of recurrent right upper quadrant pain undergoes an abdominal CT scan for an unrelated reason. The scan reveals a completely calcified gallbladder wall. What is the most significant clinical consequence of finding this 'Porcelain Gallbladder'?",
