        "question": "A 45-year-old male with a history of severe, chronic alcohol abuse presents with chronic epigastric pain and foul-smelling, floating stools (steatorrhea). Abdominal X-ray shows extensive dystrophic calcifications traversing the mid-abdomen. Destruction of the pancreatic islets in this disease will eventually lead to which complication?",
