        "question": "A 35-year-old female presents to the ER with recurrent episodes of confusion, sweating, and tremors. She is currently symptomatic, and her blood glucose is 40 mg/dL. Her symptoms resolve rapidly when given IV dextrose. Blood tests drawn during the episode show high serum insulin and high C-peptide levels. Diagnosis?",
