        "correct": 2,
        "exp": "Minimal Change Disease is the most common cause of nephrotic syndrome in children. It is mediated by T-cell cytokines that damage podocytes. Because there are no immune complexes, light microscopy and IF are completely normal. Only electron microscopy reveals the classic effacement (flattening) of podocyte foot processes.",
