        "question": "A 55-year-old Caucasian male with a history of solid tumor malignancy (lung cancer) develops nephrotic syndrome. Renal biopsy reveals thickened glomerular capillary walls. Silver stain demonstrates a classic 'spike and dome' appearance. This pattern is caused by the subepithelial deposition of which of the following?",
