        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 60-year-old patient with poorly controlled Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus presents with microalbuminuria. The primary mechanism of diabetic nephropathy involves non-enzymatic glycosylation of the vascular basement membrane. Which specific renal vessel is affected first and most severely, leading to hyperfiltration?",
