        "question": "A 50-year-old patient with poorly controlled hypertension stops taking his medications. He presents with a blood pressure of 240/140 mmHg, headache, and acute renal failure. Renal biopsy shows 'flea-bitten' hemorrhages on the cortical surface. What is the microscopic hallmark of this malignant hypertension in the renal arterioles?",
