        "question": "A 15-year-old girl presents with severe polyuria, weakness, and cramps. Labs show hypokalemia, metabolic alkalosis, and hypercalciuria. Her blood pressure is entirely normal. Genetic testing reveals an autosomal recessive defect in the Na-K-2Cl cotransporter. This condition functionally mimics the chronic use of which medication?",
