        "question": "A 30-year-old male with a history of recurrent pulmonary infections and infertility (diagnosed as Cystic Fibrosis) is found to have profound glucosuria, aminoaciduria, and phosphaturia, but his blood glucose is normal. This generalized reabsorptive defect of the Proximal Convoluted Tubule (PCT) is known as:",
