        "question": "A patient develops Acute Tubular Necrosis (ATN) following a severe crush injury (rhabdomyolysis). After the initial insult, the patient enters the 'Maintenance Phase' of ATN, characterized by severe oliguria for 1-2 weeks. What is the most dangerous, potentially fatal electrolyte imbalance that occurs during this specific phase?",
