        "exp": "The Glomerular Filtration Barrier is both a size and charge barrier. The basement membrane contains heparan sulfate, a strongly negatively charged proteoglycan. Because albumin is also negatively charged, it is repelled by the GBM. Loss of this negative charge leads to selective albuminuria (as seen in Minimal Change Disease).",
