        "exp": "Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome (WT2 gene mutation) is characterized by Wilms tumor, macroglossia, organomegaly, and hemihypertrophy (one side of the body grows larger than the other). Children with this syndrome require frequent ultrasound screening for Wilms tumor.",
