        "exp": "Xanthogranulomatous pyelonephritis is a rare, chronic granulomatous infection of the kidney, almost exclusively associated with chronic obstruction (like Staghorn calculi from Proteus infections). It destroys the kidney, replacing it with grossly yellowish tissue packed with lipid-laden (foamy) macrophages. It clinically mimics Renal Cell Carcinoma.",
