        "exp": "Cystinuria is an autosomal recessive defect in the PCT transporter responsible for reabsorbing dibasic amino acids (COLA: Cystine, Ornithine, Lysine, Arginine). Cystine is poorly soluble and precipitates, forming hexagonal crystals and kidney stones.",
