        "exp": "Alport syndrome is an X-linked dominant mutation in the COL4A5 gene, which encodes the alpha-5 chain of Type IV collagen. Without this vital structural protein, the GBM becomes fragile, splitting and separating under the pressure of filtration, leading to hematuria.",
