        "correct": 1,
        "exp": "Endocardial fibroelastosis is a rare disease found almost exclusively in infants during the first year of life. It is characterized by thick, dense, fibroelastic tissue replacing the normal endocardium, leading to a severe restrictive cardiomyopathy and early death.",
