        "exp": "Syphilitic aortitis (tertiary syphilis) is characterized by an obliterative endarteritis of the vasa vasorum. Because syphilis is a chronic infection, the inflammatory infiltrate destroying the vessels is classically composed of Plasma Cells and lymphocytes, leading to ischemia of the tunica media and 'tree-bark' wrinkling of the aorta.",
        "book": "Pathoma: Fundamentals of Pathology",
        "subtopic": "Aortic Aneurysms"
