        "exp": "In Intravascular Hemolysis (like mechanical valve shearing), RBCs are destroyed directly in the blood. The released hemoglobin binds immediately to Haptoglobin, plunging free haptoglobin levels to near zero. LDH (an intracellular RBC enzyme) leaks out, spiking serum levels. The excess free hemoglobin spills into the urine (hemoglobinuria).",
