        "question": "An infant presents with severe non-bilious projectile vomiting immediately after feeding. On physical exam, a firm, mobile, olive-like mass is palpated in the right upper quadrant. The vomiting causes the infant to lose massive amounts of gastric acid. What classic metabolic derangement will this child have?",
