        "question": "A 50-year-old male presents with generalized lymphadenopathy. A biopsy reveals a diffuse proliferation of large B-cells that obliterates the normal lymph node architecture. This is Diffuse Large B-Cell Lymphoma (DLBCL), the most common non-Hodgkin lymphoma in adults. It can arise sporadically, or it can evolve from a lower-grade lymphoma. Which indolent lymphoma is most famous for transforming into DLBCL?",
