        "exp": "Metaplasia (such as Barrett esophagus) does not occur by mature cells suddenly changing their phenotype. Instead, it is caused by the reprogramming of tissue stem cells located in the basal layer. Under chronic stress (like stomach acid), these stem cells shift their gene expression to produce a different, tougher cell type better suited to handle the new environment.",
