        "exp": "Parvovirus B19 directly infects and destroys erythroid precursors in the bone marrow. In a healthy person, this temporary halt in RBC production is unnoticeable. In a patient with Sickle Cell Anemia (whose RBCs only live 10-20 days), halting production for even a few days causes a precipitous, life-threatening drop in hemoglobin (Aplastic Crisis) marked by a near-zero reticulocyte count.",
