        "question": "A 50-year-old female with Systemic Lupus Erythematosus (SLE) presents with fatigue and jaundice. Direct Coombs test is positive. The autoantibodies causing her hemolytic anemia are of the IgG class. In which organ does the vast majority of the red blood cell destruction occur in this specific type of anemia?",
