        "question": "A 60-year-old male presents with a microcytic anemia. A bone marrow aspirate is performed and stained with Prussian Blue. The pathologist observes erythrocytes with iron-laden mitochondria forming a complete circle around the nucleus. What is the fundamental defect causing this Sideroblastic Anemia?",
