        "question": "A 25-year-old asymptomatic male of Mediterranean descent gets routine blood work. His CBC shows a mild microcytic, hypochromic anemia. Serum iron studies are completely normal. Hemoglobin electrophoresis reveals an elevation in Hemoglobin A2 (HbA2) to 5.0% (normal <3.5%). What is the diagnosis?",
