        "exp": "The PRSS1 gene encodes cationic trypsinogen. Normally, if trypsinogen is accidentally activated to trypsin inside the pancreas, a fail-safe mechanism allows the trypsin to cleave and destroy itself. The PRSS1 mutation destroys this specific cleavage site. Mutated trypsin cannot be inactivated, leading to Hereditary Pancreatitis.",
