        "question": "A 55-year-old female presents with severe pain in her mid-back that is worse when she lies flat and improves when she leans forward. An abdominal CT confirms pancreatic adenocarcinoma in the body of the pancreas. What anatomical factor explains why these tumors typically present so late and cause such severe back pain?",
