        "question": "A 55-year-old male presents with a yellowish, lobulated tumor on his eyelid. The biopsy reveals a Sebaceous Carcinoma. The physician immediately takes a thorough family history and schedules the patient for a colonoscopy. This rare exocrine skin tumor is highly associated with Muir-Torre syndrome, which is a variant of which systemic disease?",
