        "question": "A 45-year-old male with chronic pancreatitis presents with massive upper GI bleeding. Endoscopy reveals severe, bleeding gastric varices in the fundus of the stomach. However, he has NO esophageal varices and a perfectly normal liver biopsy. This localized 'left-sided portal hypertension' is caused by thrombosis of which specific vein due to pancreatic inflammation?",
