        "exp": "Psoriasis is characterized by excessive keratinocyte proliferation. The rapid turnover means cells do not have time to lose their nuclei as they reach the stratum corneum, a histological finding known as Parakeratosis (causing the silvery scales). The pinpoint bleeding when a scale is peeled off is the Auspitz sign, due to elongated dermal papillae with dilated blood vessels.",
