        "exp": "Pemphigus Vulgaris is a potentially fatal autoimmune blistering disease. IgG antibodies target Desmoglein 1 and 3 (components of desmosomes), which normally connect keratinocytes together in the stratum spinosum. This causes acantholysis (separation of epidermal cells), leaving a 'tombstone' row of basal cells attached to the basement membrane.",
