        "exp": "Bullous Pemphigoid classically affects the elderly. IgG autoantibodies target Hemidesmosomes (specifically BP180), which normally attach the basal cells of the epidermis to the underlying dermal basement membrane. Because the entire epidermis lifts off the dermis, the blister roof is thick and tense (negative Nikolsky sign), and oral mucosa is usually spared.",
