        "question": "A 35-year-old male presents with grouped, intensely pruritic vesicles on his elbows, knees, and buttocks. A skin biopsy shows microabscesses at the tips of the dermal papillae, with IgA deposition on direct immunofluorescence. The physician strongly advises the patient to eliminate which specific protein from his diet to cure the rash?",
