        "topic": "Skin Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 25-year-old female presents with a sudden eruption of 'targetoid' (bullseye-like) lesions on her palms, soles, and trunk. She recently recovered from a cold sore on her lip. What is the primary cellular mechanism driving the formation of these classic Erythema Multiforme lesions?",
