        "exp": "Erythema Multiforme (EM) is a hypersensitivity reaction characterized by targetoid lesions (a central zone of necrosis surrounded by erythema). It is most commonly triggered by an infection (especially Herpes Simplex Virus or Mycoplasma) or drugs. The lesions are formed by cytotoxic CD8+ T-cells attacking the basal cells of the epidermis.",
