        "exp": "Stevens-Johnson Syndrome (SJS) and Toxic Epidermal Necrolysis (TEN) are severe, life-threatening, drug-induced mucocutaneous reactions involving extensive epidermal sloughing. They exist on a spectrum: SJS involves <10% BSA, SJS/TEN overlap is 10-30%, and TEN involves >30% BSA. It is a medical emergency managed like severe burns.",
        "book": "Kaplan Medical USMLE Step 1 Pathology",
        "subtopic": "Inflammatory Dermatoses"
