        "question": "An obese 40-year-old female with Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus presents with thickened, hyperpigmented, 'velvety' skin in her axillae and on the back of her neck. This condition, Acanthosis Nigricans, is most commonly a cutaneous marker of which underlying systemic derangement?",
