        "question": "A 65-year-old male presents with dozens of brown, flat, 'stuck-on' appearing plaques on his back. A biopsy of one lesion reveals a benign proliferation of squamous cells with prominent keratin-filled pseudohorn cysts. The sudden, explosive onset of hundreds of these lesions (Leser-Trélat sign) is highly suspicious for:",
