        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 40-year-old male has an irregular, asymmetrical, multi-colored skin lesion excised from his back. The diagnosis is Malignant Melanoma. The pathologist must measure the 'Breslow thickness' of the tumor. Why is this specific measurement the single most important prognostic factor in melanoma?",
