        "exp": "Oculocutaneous Albinism is usually an autosomal recessive defect. Unlike Vitiligo (where melanocytes are destroyed), in Albinism, the patient has a perfectly normal NUMBER of melanocytes. However, they lack the enzyme Tyrosinase, which is required to synthesize melanin from the amino acid tyrosine.",
        "book": "Kaplan Medical USMLE Step 1 Pathology",
        "subtopic": "Pigmentation Disorders"
