        "exp": "Impetigo is a highly contagious superficial bacterial skin infection (S. aureus or S. pyogenes). It causes a classic 'honey-colored' crust. Histologically, the bacteria cause a very superficial vesicle/pustule located directly beneath the stratum corneum (subcorneal). Because it is so superficial, it ruptures easily, leaving the crust.",
