        "question": "A newborn develops a high fever, followed by a diffuse erythematous rash. Within 24 hours, the upper layers of the infant's skin begin to slough off in large sheets when touched (positive Nikolsky sign). The physician diagnoses Staphylococcal Scalded Skin Syndrome (SSSS). The exfoliative toxins (ETA and ETB) secreted by the bacteria cause this sloughing by specifically cleaving which exact protein?",
