        "question": "A 6-year-old girl presents with numerous small, firm, dome-shaped papules with a distinct central indentation (umbilication) on her trunk. A biopsy of a lesion reveals massive, eosinophilic cytoplasmic inclusions within the keratinocytes. What is the causative agent, and what are these inclusion bodies called?",
