        "exp": "Molluscum Contagiosum is caused by a Poxvirus. It presents as highly characteristic umbilicated (dimpled) papules. Because Poxviruses replicate entirely in the cytoplasm, the infected keratinocytes exhibit massive, pink, cytoplasmic viral inclusions known as Molluscum bodies (Henderson-Paterson bodies).",
