        "topic": "Skin Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A 45-year-old female complains of facial flushing, persistent erythema, and telangiectasias on her cheeks and nose. She frequently develops papules and pustules but notably has NO comedones (blackheads/whiteheads). Spicy foods and alcohol severely exacerbate her flushing. Diagnosis?",
