        "topic": "Skin Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Hard",
        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 30-year-old female presents with exquisitely tender, warm, red nodules on the anterior surfaces of both her shins. A deep incisional biopsy into the subcutaneous fat reveals inflammation strictly confined to the connective tissue septa separating the fat lobules, without causing actual necrosis of the fat cells. What is this condition?",
