        "correct": 0,
        "exp": "Erythema Nodosum is a painful, inflammatory lesion of the subcutaneous fat (a panniculitis), most classically found on the anterior shins. Histologically, it is a 'septal panniculitis' (inflammation of the septa dividing the fat lobules). It is a hypersensitivity reaction often associated with Strep infections, oral contraceptives, Sarcoidosis, or IBD.",
        "book": "Pathoma: Fundamentals of Pathology",
        "subtopic": "Panniculitis"
