        "question": "A 12-year-old wrestler develops a highly pruritic, annular (ring-shaped) erythematous plaque on his arm. The center of the lesion is clear, while the advancing border is scaly and raised. A KOH preparation of skin scrapings reveals branching, septate hyphae. What is the diagnosis?",
