        "question": "A 20-year-old healthy male living in a hot, humid climate notices irregular, hypopigmented patches on his chest and back that do not tan in the sun. A scraping treated with KOH shows a 'spaghetti and meatballs' appearance under the microscope. The organism causes hypopigmentation by producing an acid that inhibits tyrosinase. What is the organism?",
