        "exp": "Tinea (Pityriasis) Versicolor is caused by Malassezia furfur, a dimorphic yeast that is part of normal skin flora but overgrows in hot/humid conditions. The yeast degrades lipids, producing azelaic acid, which directly inhibits tyrosinase and blocks melanin synthesis. The KOH prep classically shows short hyphae and round spores ('spaghetti and meatballs').",
