        "topic": "Skin Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Harder",
        "source": "Robbins",
        "question": "A mother brings her infant to the clinic because of multiple reddish-brown macules on the child's trunk. When the physician firmly strokes one of the lesions with a tongue depressor, the lesion immediately swells, becomes a hive (urticaria), and intensely itchy (positive Darier sign). What specific cell type is proliferating in these lesions?",
