        "topic": "Skin Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Normal",
        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 10-year-old child has extremely dry, rough, scaling skin on his lower legs that resembles fish scales. The condition spares his flexural creases. The pathogenesis involves a mutation causing a deficiency in a protein that normally bundles keratin filaments and helps form the epidermal barrier. What is the deficient protein?",
