        "topic": "Skin Pathology",
        "difficulty": "Easy",
        "source": "Pathoma",
        "question": "A 6-year-old boy presents with severe sunburns after only minimal sun exposure, extreme freckling, and multiple early-onset basal cell and squamous cell carcinomas. He is diagnosed with Xeroderma Pigmentosum. This devastating autosomal recessive disease is caused by an inability to repair DNA damage. Which specific DNA repair mechanism is defective?",
