        "question": "A patient presents with superficial, easily ruptured blisters on their chest. Unlike Pemphigus Vulgaris, there is strictly NO mucosal involvement. Biopsy reveals a blister located very superficially, directly in the subcorneal layer. Immunofluorescence shows IgG autoantibodies. Which specific protein is being targeted here?",
