        "question": "A 25-year-old African American female has her earlobes pierced. Several months later, massive, thick, protuberant, claw-like masses of scar tissue grow out from the piercing sites, far exceeding the boundaries of the original wounds. Histological examination of these Keloids would reveal an intense overabundance of which specific type(s) of collagen?",
