        "question": "A 60-year-old male taking Penicillin for a severe infection develops 'palpable purpura' on his lower extremities. A skin biopsy reveals inflammation and fibrinoid necrosis of the small dermal blood vessel walls. The pathologist also notes 'nuclear dust'—fragmented debris from the nuclei of dead neutrophils. What is the pathological term for this specific finding?",
