        "question": "A newborn is found to have a patch of white hair on his forehead (a white forelock) and a depigmented patch of skin underneath it. Unlike albinism, where melanocytes are present but cannot make melanin, a skin biopsy of this child's white patch reveals a total absence of melanocytes. This autosomal dominant disorder is driven by a mutation in the c-KIT proto-oncogene. Diagnosis?",
