        "exp": "Takayasu Arteritis ('Pulseless disease') is a granulomatous vasculitis that classically affects the aortic arch and its branches in young Asian females. The severe narrowing of the great vessels leads to weak or absent pulses in the upper extremities and discrepant blood pressures between arms.",
