        "question": "An HIV-positive patient presents with red-purple skin nodules that look identical to Kaposi Sarcoma. However, a biopsy reveals that instead of a lymphocytic infiltrate, the lesions are packed with neutrophils. Silver stain demonstrates clusters of bacilli. What is the organism, and what is the disease?",
