        "question": "A 25-year-old male presents with recurrent, severe nosebleeds (epistaxis) and is found to have iron deficiency anemia. Physical exam reveals numerous blanching, spider-like red macules on his lips, oral mucosa, and fingertips. He also has a family history of GI bleeding. Diagnosis?",
