        "exp": "Hereditary Hemorrhagic Telangiectasia (Osler-Weber-Rendu syndrome) is an autosomal dominant disorder of blood vessels. It presents with multiple telangiectasias (blanching vascular lesions) on the skin and mucosal surfaces. These fragile vessels rupture easily, causing recurrent epistaxis, GI bleeds, and potentially fatal AVMs.",
