        "correct": 1,
        "exp": "HELLP syndrome (Hemolysis, Elevated Liver enzymes, Low Platelets) is a severe complication of preeclampsia/eclampsia. It is driven by systemic endothelial dysfunction leading to platelet activation, microthrombi formation in the liver (elevating enzymes), and the shearing of RBCs as they pass through the narrowed vessels (schistocytes).",
