        "exp": "A Pyogenic Granuloma is a lobulated capillary hemangioma that grows rapidly on the skin or oral mucosa. Despite the name, it is neither pyogenic (purulent) nor a granuloma. It bleeds easily and is highly associated with trauma and pregnancy (the 'pregnancy tumor').",
