        "exp": "ST elevations in leads II, III, and aVF point directly to an Inferior Wall Myocardial Infarction. In about 80-85% of people (right-dominant circulation), the inferior wall of the left ventricle is supplied by the Posterior Descending Artery, which branches off the Right Coronary Artery (RCA).",
