        "source": "Kaplan",
        "question": "A 30-year-old male presents with sudden heart failure a few weeks after a viral respiratory illness. He has a massively enlarged, 'flabby' heart with biventricular dilation. Biopsy reveals a dense lymphocytic infiltrate within the myocardium with myocyte necrosis. What is the most common viral cause of this acute condition in the US?",
