        "exp": "Viral Myocarditis is the most common cause of myocarditis in the US, and Coxsackievirus B is the most frequently implicated pathogen. It presents with a lymphocytic infiltrate (as opposed to a neutrophilic, giant cell, or eosinophilic infiltrate). It often leads to a fatal or chronic Dilated Cardiomyopathy.",
